From b30c361e955a69f6fe78c72514eadfd765359ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban_unloaded host_pass: per-sub-pass keys with
 live set and due times (H2)

host_pass ran six sub-passes unconditionally every 30 s. Each now goes through
kanban_unloaded_gates.run with its own key, so one sub-pass's inputs never gate
another. A key is made of three parts:

- the sub-pass's own input revisions: board data_version + total_changes on the
  kept reader, profile state.db revisions, replica fingerprint + remote ledger;
- frozenset(live_session_ids()), re-read after the remote wake;
- the earliest due time across its pending items: guarantee GRACE_S and
  retry_at, and the delegation 300 s recovery floor.

The keys are structural empty proofs, not caches of delivery results. A
returned [] can still mean busy, slots full, a lost claim or a swallowed error.
Any positive or unknown input is pending and runs every pass. That covers
candidate subscriptions, held/live/budget guarantee rows, busy_attempts or
non-numeric deferrals, reaped children, undelivered remote ledger rows, _woken,
and probe failures. A pending busy-chat or wake-slot deferral therefore never
skips (C11). The key is captured before the work runs. A raising sub-pass
clears its stamp. The every_store=False kill-switch path never skips.

card_change_pass stays hot by design. No cheap, complete fanout key exists:
the strict remote projection depends on alias TTL, owner freshness, ledger,
config and last-good state. A prototype proof that computed it as a probe cost
about 4x the pass it would skip (v9 replay).

Foreign-profile guarantee and killed-notice passes now read through the kept
read-only state.db handle (hermes_state_kept_reader, card I). They no longer
open a writer and reconcile the schema per profile per pass. Writes borrow the
shared writer through notice_writer. An already-delivered killed notice is
answered on the reader alone. The profile census is shared by a pass's probes
only, through a ContextVar scope.

Tests (RED on main: kanban_unloaded_gates does not exist):
- test_kanban_unloaded_gates: an unchanged empty host skips; a busy deferral
  is delivered after its due time with no other change; a guarantee backoff
  skips only until it expires; a live-set change re-runs.
- test_h2_gate_mutations (85): every key component moves only its own
  sub-pass; due-time bounds; a slot-full notice is retried every pass; a chat
  that unloads with a pending notice is reconsidered; probe failure and raising
  work leave no stamp.
- test_h2_kept_notice_readers, test_h2_killed_probe, test_h2_profile_census.

Replay (bench_h2_v9.py): synthetic 5.8k tasks / 23k sessions / 40k replica
rows, 1800 virtual s at the production 30 s cadence, base b8bed5dc vs this
change, run sequentially. See the card for the numbers.
